{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9754970669746399,"text":"In 1915, Albert Einstein was losing a war against gravity. His equations were collapsing. So at 2:00 a.m., he put down his chalk, picked up a violin, and played Mozart by candlelight while his neighbors pounded on the walls. He wasn't escaping the math. He was entering a flow state, a state we are actively killing today with AI shortcuts. Think about it. We own cars to travel fast, but we still lace up running shoes to sprint in the morning. Why? Because if the engine does all the work, our muscles rot. The same thing happens to the mind. When the shortcut replaces the climb, you get creative inflation. Efficiency goes up, human talent goes down. Right now, thousands of people are paying premium money just to lift heavy sandbags in empty sports stadiums. What that reveals about the terrifying future of art is something you aren't ready to hear.","words":[{"text":"In","start":0.06,"end":0.14,"type":"word","logprob":-0.004620233550667763},{"text":" ","start":0.14,"end":0.18,"type":"spacing","logprob":-6.198863957251888e-6},{"text":"1915,","start":0.18,"end":0.96,"type":"word","logprob":-1.6450837719617083e-6},{"text":" ","start":0.96,"end":1.12,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.00004994744449504651},{"text":"Albert","start":1.12,"end":1.48,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00004994744449504651},{"text":" ","start":1.48,"end":1.52,"type":"spacing","logprob":-3.2186455882765586e-6},{"text":"Einstein","start":1.52,"end":2.02,"type":"word","logprob":-3.2186455882765586e-6},{"text":" ","start":2.02,"end":2.12,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.0000252720492426306},{"text":"was","start":2.12,"end":2.36,"type":"word","logprob":-0.0000252720492426306},{"text":" ","start":2.36,"end":2.46,"type":"spacing","logprob":-4.887569048150908e-6},{"text":"losing","start":2.46,"end":2.86,"type":"word","logprob":-4.887569048150908e-6},{"text":" ","start":2.86,"end":2.94,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7},{"text":"a",